# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# This is not only about speed. A build context is uploaded whole to the
# daemon and every file in it can be COPYed by a later line - so a secret that
# is merely gitignored is still one `COPY . .` away from a published layer, and
# a layer is public the moment the image is. .env is listed first for that
# reason, not for its size.
#
# Everything below is either a secret, a build output that the image rebuilds
# itself, or a thing no build reads. Nothing here is a source file.

# Secrets, first and always.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build outputs. The image builds its own; copying a host's would ship whatever
# architecture the host happened to be - an amd64 jar on an arm64 Pi starts and
# then dies on the first native call.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/dist/

# Local state, none of which a build reads.
.git/
.gitignore
.githooks/
.dev-logs/
.dev-media/
.claude/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Test and tooling artefacts.
**/surefire-reports/
**/failsafe-reports/
**/jacoco.exec
**/pit-reports/
coverage/

# Editors.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
